//? Op-effect coverage guard (owner decision 2026-07-20). This is the single committed table of what
//? proves each PROPOSE_CATALOG-enabled op's REAL EFFECT (not just its param/RBAC shape — see
//? tests/unit/opCatalogParity.test.mts for that layer). Classified by a full-repo sweep over every
//? enabled op in `server/ai/opCatalog.ts`'s `ENABLED_OPS`.
//?
//? Taxonomy:
//?   - 'covered'          — a test asserts the op's real post-condition (a Prisma row created/changed/
//?                           removed, a file written, …), not just that the call returned status:success.
//?                           `ref` names the file + (where the test framework gives one) the exact test
//?                           case name that proves it.
//?   - 'excluded:infra'   — the real effect needs a live dependency this harness doesn't run (Docker,
//?                           a real git clone, a container) and no stub/fixture path exists for it. Matches
//?                           the fase-B "deferred until Docker" bucket already documented per-route.
//?   - 'excluded:external'— the real effect needs a live third-party API call (e.g. YouTube/TikTok) with
//?                           no fixture/dummy transport wired into the op's dispatch path.
//?   - 'excluded:ai-cost' — the real effect is the output of a real LLM completion (`runAiCompletion`)
//?                           with no stub provider path — asserting it for real would spend money non-
//?                           deterministically.
//?   - 'excluded:bug'      — the real effect is assertable in the current harness (no infra/external/
//?                           AI-cost blocker) but a REAL, currently-broken production bug on the op's
//?                           only real dispatch path makes it a silent no-op today, so a test would either
//?                           assert the (wrong) no-op behavior or fail honestly against broken code. `reason`
//?                           must describe the bug (file/line) and where it's documented for the fix.
//?   - 'gap'               — NOT a legal steady state (owner decision 2026-07-20, post fill-wave): every
//?                           op that is assertable in the current harness must be 'covered'. If you find
//?                           an assertable-but-untested op, either fill it or (if it's blocked by a real
//?                           bug rather than a missing test) reclassify it to 'excluded:bug' — never leave
//?                           it as 'gap'. tests/unit/opEffectCoverage.test.mts enforces zero 'gap' rows.
//?
//? tests/unit/opEffectCoverage.test.mts enforces: (a) this table's keys are EXACTLY `ENABLED_OPS` — no
//? more, no less, so a newly-enabled op with no row here goes red immediately; (b) every 'covered' ref's
//? cited file(s) exist and (where a quoted case name is given) the file's content actually contains it;
//? (c) every excluded/gap row carries a `reason`; (d) zero 'gap' rows remain.

export type EffectStatus = 'covered' | 'gap' | 'excluded:infra' | 'excluded:external' | 'excluded:ai-cost' | 'excluded:bug';

export interface EffectRow {
  status: EffectStatus;
  //? Required (by convention, enforced by the coverage test) when status === 'covered'. Free text citing
  //? the proving file(s) — quoted 'case name' substrings inside it are cross-checked against the file.
  ref?: string;
  //? Required (enforced by the coverage test) when status !== 'covered'.
  reason?: string;
}

